 visits and hospital admissions 2-7 days early vs 36% for the calendar-only ER model at the same 3% budget (95% CI +2 to +19 points). An urgent flag means about 6x the usual risk, not a prediction: about 1 in 14 is followed by an ER visit or admission within 7 days.", "erCaught": 0.467, "erCaughtCalendar": 0.363, "liftCi95Points": [2.0, 19.0], "flagPrecision": 0.074, "baseRate": 0.0119, "timesUsualRisk": 6.2, "flagsPerPatientMonth": 0.38}, "noteScan": {"baseline": "Urgent ER tier alone", "text": "Diary-note safety scan (English, Spanish, Haitian Creole word list): a red-flag note (fever or chills, can't keep fluids down, called the nurse) is followed by an ER visit or admission 27% of the time, about 23x the usual. With the urgent tier it catches 57% of ER visits 2-7 days early vs 47% for the tier alone (95% CI +6 to +15 points), for 5% more flags. No gain yet for Haitian Creole speakers: in this data their Creole notes never describe a red flag.", "erCaught": 0.566, "erCaughtUrgentOnly": 0.467, "gainCi95Points": [5.5, 14.9], "flagPrecision": 0.273, "timesUsualRisk": 23.0, "byLanguage": {"English": {"patients": 445, "er_events": 107, "calendar": 0.364, "urgent": 0.505, "urgent_or_note": 0.598}, "Haitian Creole": {"patients": 60, "er_events": 18, "calendar": 0.5, "urgent": 0.444, "urgent_or_note": 0.444}, "Spanish": {"patients": 245, "er_events": 57, "calendar": 0.316, "urgent": 0.404, "urgent_or_note": 0.544}}, "examples": [{"noteLanguage": "English", "category": "called_care_team", "note": "Called the nurse line, they said come in if it goes over 100.4", "patientId": "P00034", "erOrAdmissionWithin7Days": true}, {"noteLanguage": "English", "category": "cant_keep_fluids", "note": "Threw up twice, couldn't keep water down", "patientId": "P00080", "erOrAdmissionWithin7Days": false}, {"noteLanguage": "English", "category": "distress", "note": "Worst day so far.", "patientId": "P00034", "erOrAdmissionWithin7Days": false}, {"noteLanguage": "English", "category": "fever_infection", "note": "Chills tonight, took my temp 100.8", "patientId": "P00034", "erOrAdmissionWithin7Days": true}, {"noteLanguage": "Spanish", "category": "called_care_team", "note": "Llam\u00e9 a la enfermera, dijo que vaya si pasa de 38. Gracias a Dios por mis vecinos.", "patientId": "P02634", "erOrAdmissionWithin7Days": false}, {"noteLanguage": "Spanish", "category": "cant_keep_fluids", "note": "Vomit\u00e9 dos veces.", "patientId": "P00054", "erOrAdmissionWithin7Days": false}, {"noteLanguage": "Spanish", "category": "distress", "note": "El peor d\u00eda hasta ahora.", "patientId": "P00228", "erOrAdmissionWithin7Days": false}, {"noteLanguage": "Spanish", "category": "fever_infection", "note": "Me duele todo el cuerpo como gripe", "patientId": "P00054", "erOrAdmissionWithin7Days": false}]}, "roughPatch": {"baseline": "Calendar-only rough-patch model (treatment calendar only, same 5% alert budget)", "text": "Catches 48% of rough patches 2-7 days early vs 36% for the calendar-only rough-patch model (95% CI +8 to +15 points), at the same alert budget of about one new alert per coach per day. This lead time is shown on synthetic data only: on real people the wearable did not predict the next day (AUC 0.482).", "caught": 0.476, "caughtCalendar": 0.359, "liftCi95Points": [7.8, 15.2], "alertPrecision": 0.184, "alertPrecisionCalendar": 0.106, "alertsPerPatientMonth": 0.48, "medianLeadDays": 6.0, "alertBudget": "thresholds put 5% of quiet validation days on alert, same budget for every method", "syntheticOnly": true, "realDataNextDayAuc": 0.482}, "realData": {"text": "On real data (fatigue study, 204 people), wearables confirm a bad day but do not predict one (next-day AUC 0.482); the person's own rating does better (0.64). Proving lead time on real people needs the wearable, daily check-ins and dated ER visits and admissions for a few hundred survivors on treatment over several months; the public studies we found have the wearable and ratings but no clinical events.", "nex